      "date": "2026-11-07T09:54:09.000Z",
      "summary": "Google Research built an AI that spots signs of high blood pressure using only the pulse and motion sensors in a standard smartwatch, no cuff needed. In a 196-person study, its 65.8 percent detection rate beat the traditional in-office measurement. The method is already live in the Google Health app, though it doesn't replace a formal diagnosis. The article Google's AI detects high blood pressure from a regular smart",
      "why": "If accurate at scale, an always-on, cuffless screening in a consumer app could change how people are alerted to possible hypertension.",
      "headline": "Google AI detects high blood pressure from smartwatch",
      "aiSummary": "Google Research built an AI that spots signs of high blood pressure using only the pulse and motion sensors in a standard smartwatch, with no cuff. In a 196-person study it achieved a 65.8 percent detection rate and the feature is live in the Google Health app, though it does not replace a formal diagnosis."
